## Why it is built this way

::::::box{as=section class=features}

:::::card[Markdown first, not Markdown-shaped]{}
A document containing no HyMarkX construct renders as CommonMark plus GFM. That is not a goal,
it is a test: 692 conformance examples run as a build gate, and a regression fails the build.
:::::

:::::card[The output is proportional]{}
A document that uses no component emits no component CSS. A document with no interactive
construct emits no JavaScript at all — not a smaller runtime, none. The decorative field behind
this page's headline is a foreign component, and it costs 186 kB; the compiler made us name it
before it would emit it.
:::::

:::::card[Safe by default, not by discipline]{}
Trust mode is chosen by the host, and no construct inside a document can raise it. Expressions
cannot reach the network, storage, timers, or any host object.
:::::

::::::

## What that costs you

::::::box{as=section class=numbers}

:::::metric[conformance examples, green]{}
692
:::::

:::::metric[gzipped runtime, when used]{}
591 B
:::::

:::::metric[JavaScript for a static document]{}
0 B
:::::

:::::metric[the decorative hero, gzipped]{}
186 kB
:::::

:::::metric[packages, one boundary each]{}
7
:::::

::::::

::::::box{as=section class=start #start}

## Start

```sh
npm install hymarkx
npx hmx build index.md --out dist
```

`hmx` also gives you `check`, `fmt`, and a `dev` server with live reload. There is a
[VS Code extension](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=name0x0.hymarkx) with a
language server behind it — diagnostics, completion, hover, and formatting.

